hadiths[134]{hadithnumber,text}:
"494","It was narrated from Ibn Shihab that 'Umar bin 'Abdul-'Aziz delayed the 'Asr prayer a little. 'Urwah said to him:""Jibril came down and led the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in prayer."" 'Umar said: ""Watch what you are saying"
"495","Shu'bah said:""Sayyar bin Salamah"
"496","It was narrated from Az-Zuhri he said:""Anas told me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out when the sun had passed its zenith"
"497","It was narrated that Khabbab said:""We complained to the Messenger of Alalh (ﷺ) about how hot the sand was"
"498","Hamzah Al-'A'idhi said:""I heard Anas bin Malik say: 'When the Prophet (ﷺ) halted"
"499","Khalid bin Dinar Abu Khaldah said:""I heard Anas bin Malik say: 'When it was hot"
"500","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'If it is very hot"
"501","It was narrated from Abu Musa in a Marfu' [1] report:""Wait until it cools down to pray Zuhr"
"502","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: This is 'Jibril"
"503","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud said:""The Prophet (ﷺ) prayed Zuhr when the length of (a person's shadow) was between three and five feet in summer"
"504","It was narrated that Jabir said:""A man asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the times of prayer. He said: 'Pray with me.' So he prayed Zuhr when the sun had passsed its zenith"
"505","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed 'Asr when the sun was in her room and the shadow had not appeared on her wall"
"506","It was narrated from Anas:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to pray 'Asr"
"507","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to pray 'Asr when the sun was still high and bright"
"508","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to lead us in 'Asr prayer when the sun was still bright and high"
"509","It was narrated that Abu Bakr bin 'Uthman bin Sahl bin Hunaif said:""I heard Abu Umamah bin Sahl say: 'We prayed Zuhr with 'Umar bin 'Abdul-'Aziz"
"510","It was narrated that Abu Salamah said:""We prayed at the time of 'Umar bin 'Abdul-'Aziz"
"511","Al-'Ala' narrated to us that he entered upon Anas bin Malik in his house in Al-Basrah"
"512","It was narrated from Salim"
"513","It was narrated from Jabir bin 'Abdullah that Jibril came to the Prophet (ﷺ) to teach him the times of prayer. Jibril went forward"
"514","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah"
"515","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:""Whoever catches up with one Rak'ah of 'Asr prayer before the sun sets"
"516","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:""If any one of you catches the first prostration of 'Asr prayer before the sun sets"
"517","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""Whoever catches up with a Rak'ah of the Subh prayer before the sun rises"
"518","It was narrated from Nasr bin 'Abdur-Rahman"
"519","It was narrated from Sulaiman bin Buraidah that his father said:""A man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and asked him about the times of prayer. He said: 'Stay with us for these two days.' Then he told Bilal to say the Iqamah at dawn and he prayed Fajr. Then he told him to do that when the sun had passed its zenith and he prayed Zuhr. Then he told him to do that when the sun was still bright"
"520","It was narrated from a man of Aslam"
"521","It was narrated that Abu Basrah Al-Ghifari said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) led us in praying 'Asr in Al-Mukhammas. He said: 'This prayer was enjoined upon those who came before you"
"522","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Amr - and (one of the narrators) Shu'bah said:""Sometimes he (Qatadah"
"523","Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa narrated that his father said:""A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) asking him about the times of prayer"
"524","Al-Husain bin Bashir bin Sallam narrated that his father said:""Muhammad bin 'Ali and I entered upon Jabir bin 'Abdullah Al-Ansari. We said to him: 'Tell us about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).' That was at the time of Al-Hajjaj bin Yusuf. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out and prayed Zuhr when the sun had passed its zenith and the shadow (of a thing) was the length of a sandal-strap. Then he prayed 'Asr when the shadow of a man was the length of a sandal-strap plus his height. Then he prayed Maghrib when the sun had set. Then he prayed 'Isha' when the twilight disappeared. Then he prayed Fajr when dawn broke. The next day he prayed Zuhr when a man's shadow was equal to his height. Then he prayed 'Asr when a man's shadow was twice his height"
"525","Sayyar bin Salamah said:""I entered upon Abu Barzah"
"526","Jabir bin 'Abdullah said:""Jibril"
"527","It was narrated that Muhammad bin 'Amr bin Hasan said:""Al-Hajjaj arrived"
"528","It was narrated that An-Nu'man bin Bashir said:""I am the most knowledgeable of people about the time of the 'Isha' prayer. The Prophet (ﷺ) used to pray it when the moon set on the third night of the month"
"529","It was narrated that An-Nu'man bin Bashir said:""By Allah"
"530","Sayyar bin Salamah said:""My father and I entered upon Abu Barzah"
"531","It was narrated that Ibn Juraij said:""I said to 'Ata': 'What is the best time you think I should pray Al-'Atamah"
"532","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""The Prophet (ﷺ) delayed 'Isha' one night until part of the night had passed. Then 'Umar"
"533","It was narrated that Jabir bin Samurah said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to delay the later 'Isha'.""[1] [1] It is described as the later 'Isha' prayer because the Maghrib prayer is sometimes called 'Isha' prayer"
"534","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""Were it not that I would impose too much difficulty on my Ummah"
"535","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delayed A;-'Atamah one night"
"536","It was narrated that 'Aishah the Mother of the Believers said:""The Prophet (ﷺ) delayed the prayer one night until most of the night had passed and the people in the Masjid had gone home to sleep"
"537","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:""We stayed in the Masjid one night waiting for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to pray 'Isha'. He came out to us when one-third of the night or more had passed"
"538","It was narrated that Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) led us in Maghrib prayer"
"539","Humaid said:""Anas was asked: 'Did the Prophet (ﷺ) use a ring?' He said: 'Yes. One night he delayed the later 'Isha' prayer"
"540","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""If the people knew what (virtue) there was in the call to prayer and the first row"
"541","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Do not let the Bedouin make you change the name of this prayer of yours"
"542","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say on the Minbar: 'Do not let the Bedouin make you change the name of your prayer; verily"
"543","Ja'far bin Muhammad bin 'Ali bin Al-Husain narrated from his father"
"544","Humaid narrated from Ans that a man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and asked him about the time of the Subh prayer. The following morning he commanded that the Iqamah for prayer be said when dawn broke"
"545","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:""When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has prayed Subh"
"546","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:""The women used to pray Subh with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"547","It was narrated that Anas said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed Fajr on the day of Khaibar during the time it was still dark"
"548","It was narrated from Rafi' bin Khadij that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:""Pray Fajr when the dawn shines"
"549","It was narrated from Mahmud bin Labid"
"550","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:""Whoever catches up with a prostration of Subh before the sun rises"
"551","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:""Whoever catches up with a Rak'ah of Fajr before the sun rises"
"552","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to pray Zuhr when the sun passed its zenith"
"553","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""Whoever catches up with a Rak'ah of the prayer"
"554","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""Whoever catches up with a Rak'ah of the prayer"
"555","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:""Whoever catches up with a Rak'ah of the prayer"
"556","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever catches up with a Rak'ah of the prayer has caught up with it"
"557","It was narrated from Salim"
"558","It was narrated from Salim that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""Whoever catches up with a Rak'ah of one of the prayers has caught up with it"
"559","It was narrated from 'Abdullah As-Sunabihi that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""The sun rises and with it the horn of the Shaitan"
"560","It was narrated that Musa bin 'Ali bin Rabah said:""I heard my father say: 'I heard 'Uqbah bin 'Amir Al-Juhani say: There are three times during which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade us to pray in or bury our dead: When the sun has clearly stated to rise"
"561","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade praying after 'Asr until the sun had set"
"562","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""I heard more than one of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) - including 'Umar who was one of the dearest of them to me - that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade praying after Fajr until the sun had risen"
"563","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""No one of you should deliberately try to pray when the sun is rising"
"564","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade praying when the sun is rising or setting"
"565","It was narrated from Musa bin 'Ali that his father said:""I heard 'Uqbah bin 'Amir say: 'There are three times during which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade us from praying or burying our dead: When the sun had clearly started to rise until it was fully risen"
"566","It was narrated from Damrah bin Sa'eed that he heard Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri say:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade praying after Subh until the sun had risen"
"567","It was narrated from 'Ata' bin Yazid that he heard Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri say:""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'There is no prayer after Fajr until the sun has clearly risen"
"568","(Another chain) from Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri"
"569","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade praying after 'Asr"
"570","It was narrated from Ibn Tawus that his father said:""'Aishah"
"571","Ibn 'Umar said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'When the edge of the sun rises"
"572","Abu Yahya Sulaim bin 'Amir"
"573","It was narrated that 'Ali said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)forbade praying after 'Asr unless the sun was still white"
"574","It was narrated that Hisham said:""My father told me: 'Aishah said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never neglected to pray two Rak'ahs after 'Asr in my house"
"575","It was narrated that Al-Aswad said:'Aishah said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never entered upon me after 'Asr but he prayed them (the two Rak'ahs)"
"576","It was narrated that Abu Ishaq said:""I heard Masruq and Al-Aswad say: We bear witness that 'Aishah said: 'When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was with me after 'Asr"
"577","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:""There are two prayers that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never neglected to pray them in my house secretly nor publicly: Two Rak'ahs before Fajr and two Rak'ahs after 'Asr"
"578","It was narrated from Abu Salamah that he asked 'Aishah about the two prostrations (Rak'ahs) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to pray after 'Asr. She said:""He used to pray them before 'Asr"
"579","It was narrated from Umm Salamah that the Prophet (ﷺ) once prayed two Rak'ahs after 'Asr in her house. She asked him about that and he said:""They are two Rak'ahs that I used to pray after Zuhr"
"580","It was narrated that Umm Salamah said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) got distracted and did not pray the two Rak'ahs before 'Asr so he prayed them after 'Asr"
"581","Imran bin Hudair said:""I asked Lahiq about the two Rak'ahs before sunset. He said: ""Abdullah bin Az-Zubair used to pray them"
"582","It was narrated from Yazid bin Abi Habib that Abu Al-Khair told him:""Abu Tamim Al-Jaishani stood up to pray two Rak'ahs before Maghrib"
"583","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that Hafsah said:""When the dawn appears"
"584","It was narrated that 'Amr bin 'Abasah said:""I came to the Messenger of Allah"
"585","It was narrated from Jubair bin Mut'im that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:""O Banu 'Abd Manaf"
"586","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:""If the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was setting out on a journey before the sun passed its zenith"
"587","It was narrated from Abu At-Tufail 'Amir bin Wathilah that Mu'adh bin Jabal told him that they went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the year of Tabuk"
"588","Kathir bin Qarawanda said:""I asked Salim bin 'Abdullah about how his father prayed when traveling. We asked him: 'Did he combine any of his prayers when traveling?' He said that Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubaid was married to him"
"589","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""I prayed with the Prophet (ﷺ) in Al-Madinah"
"590","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that he prayed Al-Uula (Zuhr) and 'Asr together in Al-Basrah with nothing in between them"
"591","It was narrated that Isma'il bin 'Abdur-Rahman"
"592","It was narrated that Az-Zuhri said:""Salim told me that his father said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"593","It was narrated that Jabir said:""The sun set when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was in Makkah"
"594","It was narrated from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""If the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wanted to travel quickly"
"595","Nafi' said:""I went out with 'Abdullah bin 'Umar on a journey to some of his land. Then someone came to him and said: 'Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubaid is sick"
"596","It was narrated that Nafi' said:""We came back with Ibn 'Umar from Makkah. One night he kept on travelling until evening came"
"597","Kathir bin Qarawanda said:""We asked Salim bin 'Abdullah about prayer while traveling. We said: 'Did 'Abdullah combine any of his prayer while traveling?' He said: 'No"
"598","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that if the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was in a hurry to travel"
"599","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:""If the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was in a hurry to travel"
"600","Sufyan said:""I heard Az-Zuhri say: 'Salim told me that his father said: 'I saw the Prophet (ﷺ)"
"601","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed Zuhr and 'Asr together"
"602","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to pray in Al-Madinah combining two prayer. Joining Zuhr and 'Asr"
"603","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) eight (Rak'ahs) together and seven (Rak'ahs) together"
"604","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrated from his father that Jabir bin 'Abdullah said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) traveled until he came to 'Arafah"
"605","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin Yazid that Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari told him"
"606","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Jubair said:""I was with Ibn 'Umar when he departed from 'Arafah. When he came to Jam' (Al-Muzdalifah)"
"607","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Prophet (ﷺ) prayed Maghrib and 'Isha' at Al-Muzdalifah"
"608","It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:""I never saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) combine any two prayers except in Al-Muzdalifah"
"609","It was narrated from Usamah bin Zaid"
"610","Al-Walid bin Al'Ayzar said:""I heard Abu 'Amr Ash-Shaibani say: 'The owner of this house - and he pointed to the house of 'Abdullah - said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): 'Which deed is most beloved to Allah"
"611","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud said:""I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) which action is most beloved to Allah? He said: 'Establishing prayer on time"
"612","It was narrated from Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir that his father was in the Masjid of 'Amr bin Shurahbil and the Iqamah for prayer was said"
"613","It was narrated that Anas said:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever forgets a prayer"
"614","It was narrated that Anas said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about a man who slept and missed the prayer"
"615","It was narrated that Abu Qatadah said:""They told the Prophet (ﷺ) that they had slept and missed the prayer. He said: 'There is no negligence when one sleeps"
"616","It was narrated that Abu Qatadah said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'There is no negligence when one sleeps"
"617","It was narrated from Abu Qatadah that when they missed the prayer because they slept until the sun rose"
"618","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: If you forget a prayer"
"619","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""Whoever forgets a prayer"
"620","It was narrated from Ma'mar"
"621","It was narrated from Buraid bin Abi Mariam that his father said:""We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a journey"
"622","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud said:""We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and we were prevented from praying Zuhr"
"623","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""We stopped to camp at the end of the night with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"624","It was narrated from Nafi' bin Jubair"
"625","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set out at nightfall"
"626","Nafi' narrated that 'Abdullah bin 'Umar used to say:""When the Muslims arrived in Al-Madinah they used to gather and try to figure out the time for prayer"
"627","It was narrated that Anas said:""The Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) commanded Bilal to say the phrases of the Adhan twice and the phrases of the Iqamah once"